            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Six-Day War 1967</strong><br>\nIn 1967, the Six-Day War took place, in which Israel gained control over the West Bank, the Gaza Strip, the Golan Heights, and the Sinai Peninsula. This considerably expanded Israel's territory and led to the occupation of Palestinian areas.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Yom Kippur War 1973</strong><br>\nIn 1973, the Yom Kippur War broke out, in which Egypt and Syria surprisingly attacked Israel. Despite initial losses, Israel was able to repel the attackers and hold the occupied territory.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Camp David Accords 1978</strong><br>\nIn 1978, the Camp David Accords were signed between Egypt, Israel, and the United States. Egypt recognized Israel and, in return, Israel gave back the Sinai Peninsula. This was an initial step toward normalizing relations in the region.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
