            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>First Intifada 1987-1993</strong><br>\nIn 1987, the First Intifada began, a Palestinian uprising against Israeli occupation. This led to talks and eventually to the signing of the Oslo Accords, which provided some autonomy for the Palestinians.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Second Intifada 2000-2005</strong><br>\nThe Second Intifada broke out in the year 2000 and was characterized by suicide bombings and intense clashes. The conflict heightened tensions between Israelis and Palestinians and significantly hindered the peace process.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Ongoing Peace Efforts</strong><br>\nSince then, there have been several attempts to revive the peace process between Israel and Palestine. Despite international mediation and some progress, the situation remains complex, and the path to a lasting solution is still long.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
